Subject: [overlay 0023] visionOS VR — gamepad aim/turn, the alignment chain, the 2D redirect

The R2 engine delta, gated on the same q2vr state block overlay 0022 introduced, so every
other configuration — iOS, the macOS oracle, the visionOS 2D window, the visionOS 3D panel —
leaves it zero and takes byte-for-byte the paths it takes today.

  * q2_vr_state_t gains an APPENDED R2 section (shared.h): the absolute aim source, the
    movement-direction rotation, the standing-height rise and its clamp result, the two
    values the client publishes back, and the 2D-redirect gate. Appended and not inserted:
    the shell and the engine are separate translation units that agree only by layout.

  * ABSOLUTE AIM (client/input.c, CL_UpdateCmd). cl.viewangles is what the client SENDS;
    the VR camera comes from the published head pose, so writing the head's angles here
    gives stock progs, mods, the campaign and multiplayer ordinary view angles with no
    protocol change. ASSIGNED, never accumulated — cl_ios_look_delta is a delta accumulator
    that composes with touch and gyro. Placed before CL_ClampPitch so the SENT pitch still
    gets the engine's +-89 clamp while the RENDER pitch stays the head's true one, and
    outside CL_AdjustAngles because that function early-returns while the weapon wheel is
    open (which would leave aim dead exactly while the player is choosing a weapon).
    cl.viewangles is published back as q2vr.view_yaw_out/view_pitch_out so the shell can
    seed its body yaw from the game's own facing rather than from 0.

  * MOVEMENT DIRECTION (client/input.c, CL_FinalizeCmd) — the FINISHED wish vector rotated
    after every device has contributed and after the speed clamp. Two lines of trig, no
    protocol change. The sign of the side term is not the textbook rotation: the server
    builds velocity as F*forwardmove + R*sidemove with R 90 degrees CLOCKWISE of F.

  * STANDING HEIGHT + CEILING CLAMP (client/view.c, client/entities.c). The rise is applied
    in WORLD Z, not along the head's own up axis — a player's stature does not tilt when
    they tilt their head. CL_VR_ClampRise traces up with the existing CL_LerpedTrace and
    clamps asymmetrically: DUCK INSTANTLY (a frame rendered from inside a brush is a visible
    defect), RISE BACK EASED at ~40 u/s (a camera that snaps upward is the one motion the
    head did not ask for). Eased once per host FRAME, not once per eye.

  * THE VR YAW COMPOSITION, corrected (client/view.c is unchanged here; the shell now
    contributes zero head yaw while aim is live). Documented in q2_vr_input.m: the head yaw
    goes OUT through cl.viewangles and comes BACK through cl.predicted_angles, so adding it
    at the render site as well would double every head turn — and reading the game's own
    view yaw is what makes teleports and spawn re-orientation rotate the camera too.

  * THE 2D REDIRECT (client/screen.c) — the whole 2D stream (HUD, UI_Draw, console, notify,
    loading plaque, and the weapon wheel's own capture, which rides SCR_Draw2D) is drawn
    ONCE per host frame into a UI framebuffer instead of into the eye image. Two bind/unbind
    brackets rather than one, because V_RenderView sits between the HUD half and the
    menu/console half and the WORLD must land in the eye target. The hooks are function
    POINTERS in q2vr, not extern functions, so no configuration without a platform shell
    (the macOS oracle, the meson build) needs a stub to link.

    NOT redirected, deliberately: the pre-world 2D siblings inside SCR_DrawActive (the black
    fill for a non-active client, the cinematic blit, SCR_TileClear). Every one belongs to a
    frame arbitration has already sent to the PANEL — a VR world frame is ca_active,
    non-cinematic and runs at viewsize 100 — so redirecting them would move nothing and put
    a bind/unbind pair on the world path for no reason.

Apply: patch -p1 -d vendor/q2repro < this
